mittee":"Council","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.n-kesteven.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-02","committee":"Resources Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"New","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.n-kesteven.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-03","committee":"Executive Board","time":"3.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.n-kesteven.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-04","committee":"Flourishing Communities Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"New","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.n-kesteven.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-13","committee":"Resources Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"New","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.n-kesteven.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-20","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.n-kesteven.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-23","committee":"Executive Board","time":"3.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.n-kesteven.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-14","committee":"Resources Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.n-kesteven.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"Flourishing Communities Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.n-kesteven.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Repairs contractor Ian Williams has 84% upheld complaint rate; dominates contractor complaints","lead":"High upheld rates mean valid service failures are confirmed; concentrated complaints against one contractor indicates contract performance failure requiring immediate action, whether through remediation demands or contract termination.","iso":"2026-09-14","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Complaints Performance Data","paper_url":"https://democracy.n-kesteven.gov.uk/documents/s157939/157939.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Local Authority complaints more than doubled in Q1","lead":"An unexplained complaints surge signals either real service failure or breakdown in complaint management. Either case creates financial risk through compensation, service recovery costs, and governance scrutiny from elected members and external audit.","iso":"2026-09-14","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Complaints Performance Data","paper_url":"https://democracy.n-kesteven.gov.uk/documents/s157939/157939.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Bin collection complaints spike 16-fold in Q1 2026/27","lead":"A statutory service with this complaint volume signals operational risk and reputational damage. Could trigger unbudgeted costs for service recovery, contractor disputes, staff time, or compensation claims.","iso":"2026-09-14","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Complaints Performance Data","paper_url":"https://democracy.n-kesteven.gov.uk/documents/s157939/157939.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"Resources Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Complaints Performance Data","paper_url":"https://democracy.n-kesteven.gov.uk/documents/s157939/157939.pdf","headline":"Repairs contractor Ian Williams has 84% upheld complaint rate; dominates contractor complaints","detail":"Q1 2026/27: 19 complaints against Ian Williams with 84.21% upheld rate (vs overall repairs service 76.47% and competitor Sureserve 66.67%). Ian Williams accounts for 19 of 34 total contractor complaints (56%), indicating one contractor is responsible for majority of complaints.","category":"other","matters":"High upheld rates mean valid service failures are confirmed; concentrated complaints against one contractor indicates contract performance failure requiring immediate action, whether through remediation demands or contract termination.","figures":"Q1 2026/27: 19 complaints against Ian Williams, 84.21% upheld","quote":"Ian Williams Ltd 26 19 25 14 22 87 19","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"Resources Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Complaints Performance Data","paper_url":"https://democracy.n-kesteven.gov.uk/documents/s157939/157939.pdf","headline":"Local Authority complaints more than doubled in Q1","detail":"Non-landlord complaints to the council jumped from 23 to 54 in Q1, a 135% increase. This broad spike across multiple service areas (building control, planning enforcement, customer services, environmental protection) suggests either genuine service deterioration or loss of control over complaint handling processes.","category":"governance","matters":"An unexplained complaints surge signals either real service failure or breakdown in complaint management. Either case creates financial risk through compensation, service recovery costs, and governance scrutiny from elected members and external audit.","figures":"Q1 2025/26: 23 complaints; Q1 2026/27: 54 complaints","quote":"Local Authority Complaints Received (Stage 1) 23 54","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"Resources Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Complaints Performance Data","paper_url":"https://democracy.n-kesteven.gov.uk/documents/s157939/157939.pdf","headline":"Bin collection complaints spike 16-fold in Q1 2026/27","detail":"Waste service complaints jumped from 1 in Q1 2025/26 to 16 in Q1 2026/27. Waste is a statutory service; this 1,500% increase indicates either contractor failure, a new contractor in difficulty, or significant service degradation that has triggered mass complaints.","category":"demand","matters":"A statutory service with this complaint volume signals operational risk and reputational damage. Could trigger unbudgeted costs for service recovery, contractor disputes, staff time, or compensation claims.","figures":"Q1 2025/26: 1 complaint; Q1 2026/27: 16 complaints","quote":"WSS - bin collection 1 16 15","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"Resources Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Key Performance Indicators","paper_url":"https://democracy.n-kesteven.gov.uk/documents/s157906/157906.pdf","headline":"Arts KPIs missing recent data for three priority demographic measures under new GLL management","detail":"Three key performance indicators for arts participation among over-65s, residents with disabilities, and priority ward residents show 'No Data' for 2024/25 and 2025/26 under GLL's management, where they were previously tracked.","category":"governance","matters":"Loss of monitoring data for vulnerable populations indicates either service disruption or failed contract oversight. If the council cannot measure outcomes for target groups, contract management is impaired.","figures":"Three KPIs with no data recorded for 2024/25 and 2025/26","quote":"KPI 3.1 Residents over 65 (22,492) taking part in an arts activity once per year. No Data No data","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"Resources Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Key Performance Indicators","paper_url":"https://democracy.n-kesteven.gov.uk/documents/s157906/157906.pdf","headline":"Under-16 participation at GLL fell 41% in 2024/25 and remains 31% below 2023/24 baseline","detail":"Youth participation dropped from 211,090 in 2023/24 to 124,086 in 2024/25, then recovered only to 144,905 in 2025/26. The sustained gap below prior baseline indicates ongoing loss of youth engagement.","category":"demand","matters":"Youth engagement is a stated council priority outcome. A sustained 31% reduction suggests either loss of access (facility closures, price increases) or declining appeal requiring intervention.","figures":"211,090 (2023/24), 124,086 (2024/25), 144,905 (2025/26)","quote":"Under 16's usage of NKDC-owned or operated leisure facilities. 227,058 211,090 124,086 144,905","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-14"},"name":"North Kesteven","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-17","since_iso":"2026-08-18","distress":false,"headline":"Repairs contractor Ian Williams has 84% upheld complaint rate; dominates contractor complaints","lead":"High upheld rates mean valid service failures are confirmed; concentrated complaints against one contractor indicates contract performance failure requiring immediate action, whether through remediation demands or contract termination.","also":["25 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Executive Board on 2026-09-17","n_findings":26,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Complaints Performance Data","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.n-kesteven.gov.uk/documents/s157939/157939.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":57,"news_drafts_total":3}}